  "pinned": false,
  "notes": "PARTIALLY PINNED. The runtime closure is pinned byte for byte: every wheel below is named, sized and hashed from pypi.org, resolved for windows-x86_64-cp313 -- the platform this was first tested on. The DPDFNet model is DECLARED BUT NOT HASHED: the machine that wrote this manifest could not reach huggingface.co, so the model's size and digest are recorded at install time from what the publisher actually serves, and its revision is the publisher's branch rather than an immutable commit. That is a weaker claim than the closure's and the difference is worth stating: an artifact with a digest here is checked against a number this repository committed to, and one without is checked against the digest its publisher reports at install time. Both refuse a file that arrives wrong; only the first refuses a publisher who changed their mind. A stage in that state carries \"provisional\": true, the settings row says so in words, and `python tools/pin_pipeline_models.py --stage dpdfnet --revision <sha>` on a machine that can reach the hub turns the first claim into the second. LavaSR is not installable in this build at all -- see its own entry.",
