    "attribution": "Resolved from PyPI for CPython 3.13 on Windows x86-64 with pip's own resolver, then hashed and checked against the digests pypi.org publishes for each file.",
    "closure_notes": "The enhancement runtime is deliberately NOT PocketTTS's interpreter (section 14.6). Lifecycle coupling does not imply dependency coupling: Pocket's closure stays reproducible, the pipeline can later serve Kokoro and Sopro, and a pipeline update cannot mutate the environment a working voice depends on. The closure below is the ONNX path -- Path A of section 10.4 -- which is the one to validate first because it shares a runtime with DPDFNet and gives explicit thread control. If Phase 0 rejects it, section 14.5 says to use the official PyTorch/Vocos LavaSR in this same isolated runtime with a project-owned rate adapter, which is a different closure and a different 'build' number here, not a different design.",
