      "contract": {
        "package": "dpdfnet",
        "model_id": "dpdfnet8_48khz_hr",
        "model_sample_rate": 48000,
        "accepts_any_input_rate": true,
        "output_rate": null,
        "notes": "Measured from upstream 0.6.0's own source rather than from its README. StreamEnhancer.process(chunk, sample_rate=N) resamples N to the model's native rate internally and returns output back at N, so the stage is handed Pocket's real 24000 Hz and gives back 24000 Hz -- output_rate is null because this stage's output rate is its caller's, and the 48 kHz in the model name is the network's own working rate. The streaming path is a causal STFT that upstream documents as deliberately NOT bit-identical to its offline enhance(); that is the correct path for real time and is the one this feature uses. onnx_path is passed explicitly so resolve_model() never reaches the network (I-VP-22)."
      },
      "provisional": true
    },
